// A body whose exit GATE carries its order in the values it reads rather than in a wait edge
// (`Builder::layRegionWriteEdges`): the region hands `0` out and keeps `println(1)` alive after it,
// so the exit is a GATE whose ordinary inputs are `[0, println]` -- two of them, and the node has
// no sync predecessor and no control input at all.
//
// This is the shape `core.arrangeable` refuses: its four terms are all true (it is pure, it reaches
// nothing, it cannot fault and it ends) and it is still not freely arrangeable, because the order a
// gate stands in is not one of the four terms and is exactly what a pass must not be free to move.
// The program is otherwise plain -- no call, no branch, no `for` loop, no conversion -- so the gate
// is the one node whose answer the census has to carry, and the values beside it are the control
// that the answer is a reading of the node and not a constant.
//
// `main` returns `0` and not the value it hands on: a program's exit status is `main`'s value, and
// this case is read by a test that expects exit 0.
//
// Run: camel test/cases/facts/a_body_exit_gate_reads_its_writes.cml test::facts_compare
func main() => int {
    println(1)
    return 0
}
